= TestConfigurationRelease

Everything in this folder except this file is *generated* by
`buildScripts/create_test_configuration_release.py` and is not committed. Do not edit it by
hand: change the source data in `Instance/` or the test configuration definition instead.

This is level 1 of the two-level release process (issue #332). Level 2, the package release,
is built by `.github/workflows/release_packages.yml` when a GitHub Release is published.

== Test configurations

Each test configuration is defined by `buildScripts/test_configurations/<Name>.toml`, which
lists the `Instance/` files it needs as include/exclude globs. A test configuration contains
only the files its test requires; each test refers to the release it uses.

[cols="1,3"]
|===
| Name | Purpose

| FullReliCapGridBaseCase
| The complete ReliCapGrid dataset: imported in full and used to run a power flow on the
complete model.
|===

== Layout

----
<Name>/
├── manifest.xml               DCAT manifest (RDF/XML), written with CimPal
├── manifest.trig              the same manifest as TriG
├── manifest.json              the same manifest as JSON-LD
├── sources.json               release path -> Instance/ source path
└── instance/
    ├── Grid/                  IGM and RCC (Jotunheim) grid datasets
    ├── NetworkCode/           network code profile datasets
    ├── boundaryData/
    ├── commonData/
    └── referenceData/
        └── <serialisation>/   cimxml or ttl (source format), trig, jsonld
            └── <timestamp>_<source file name>
----

* All files of one release share the build time as filename prefix (`20261118T1030Z_`).
* `cimxml` / `ttl` files are byte-for-byte copies of the sources, so intentionally invalid
  (negative) test data is kept exactly as authored.
* `trig` / `jsonld` files are re-serialised with rdflib. The named graph is the dataset
  header IRI; relative CIM identifiers `#_<uuid>` become `urn:uuid:<uuid>`. Files that cannot
  be parsed are shipped in their source format only, with a warning.
* The manifest describes every dataset with one distribution per serialisation; `dcat:accessURL`
  is relative to the release folder.
* Previous output of a test configuration is removed before it is regenerated.

== Generating and validating

[source,bash]
----
python buildScripts/create_test_configuration_release.py --cimpal-jar <path>/CimPal-CLI.jar
uv run buildScripts/validate_instances.py --apl cgmes-3.0=.apl-cgmes --apl ncp-2.5=.apl-ncp \
  --release TestConfigurationRelease/FullReliCapGridBaseCase
----

The source data is not validated directly, as it may contain negative test cases; validation
runs on the generated release. CI (`.github/workflows/shacl_validation.yml`) generates and
validates `FullReliCapGridBaseCase` on every push that touches the data or these scripts, and
uploads the release as a workflow artifact.
